WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.659 --> 00:00:04.019
Shakespeare had written of course very famously that all the world's a stage

00:00:04.180 --> 00:00:09.570
right? And that's really the kind of picture of metaphor that Newton has in mind throughout his greatest work "The Principia"

00:00:09.639 --> 00:00:15.059
The planets will move around, the comets will orbit the sun, the apples will fall, and all that happens, all that action

00:00:15.309 --> 00:00:21.839
Takes place on a kind of perfectly rigid, unchanging stage. That stage is then space and time for Newton

00:00:21.960 --> 00:00:25.710
So Newton says very famously space and time are each absolute. They flow without

00:00:26.410 --> 00:00:30.389
Compromise, there's nothing that happens on that stage is going to affect the stage itself

00:00:31.360 --> 00:00:32.920
They're not actors in the drama

00:00:32.920 --> 00:00:35.840
Newton's view of time is

00:00:36.040 --> 00:00:40.740
the what I would call the everyday notion of time that we

00:00:41.860 --> 00:00:48.239
That we grow up with, that we become familiar with in our everyday lives: the notion that time is universal

00:00:48.239 --> 00:00:50.699
It's the same for everyone,

00:00:51.370 --> 00:00:57.149
Everywhere no matter what they're doing,  that it ticks away at a constant rate and time is passing

00:00:58.030 --> 00:00:59.559
equally and

00:00:59.559 --> 00:01:02.279
exactly the same for everyone no matter what they're doing and

00:01:03.489 --> 00:01:07.649
All of our everyday experience points to this being the correct notion of time

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:11.620
And we come to, to, Einstein and especially with his general theory of relativity

00:01:12.880 --> 00:01:14.500
his theory of Gravity

00:01:14.500 --> 00:01:18.449
Space and time were their union into space time now has become an actor in the play

00:01:18.490 --> 00:01:24.269
it's not sort of set off apart from the other things like the planets whizzing around or comets or apples

00:01:24.270 --> 00:01:28.200
It's now part of that story so that the other actors say large

00:01:28.930 --> 00:01:32.790
masses like the Sun can actually have an impact that can affect the

00:01:32.860 --> 00:01:36.360
shape of space the flow of time in its vicinity and vice versa

00:01:36.579 --> 00:01:39.599
So they become part of the kind of stage play not set off

00:01:39.880 --> 00:01:46.019
So Newton had said time and space were first of all separate from each other and were sort of absolute apart

00:01:46.240 --> 00:01:50.100
Distinct and Einstein starts folding them in to the kind of larger drama

00:01:50.649 --> 00:01:55.079
In Einstein's theory of gravity time, becomes personal

00:01:55.540 --> 00:02:00.419
So the time that elapses for me is entirely personal to me the time

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:03.820
elapses for anyone is entirely personal to them and

00:02:04.520 --> 00:02:06.520
the way that time

00:02:07.040 --> 00:02:09.729
Elapses, the way that time flows for an individual is

00:02:10.520 --> 00:02:13.719
Completely dependent on where they are and what they're doing

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:21.970
So if all the world's a stage, then the structure of that stage is the structure of space-time this entity that that Einstein introduced

